{"type":"npc","name":"Scupa","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":80,"temp":0,"max":80,"details":""},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":15}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"electricity","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"mental","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aetheran","astral","common","diabolic","draconic","empyrean","utopian"],"details":""},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Scupas resemble mechanical peacocks with multi-colored tails. They dedicate their lives to bringing order and beauty to places that were once chaotic and destroyed, and they pride themselves on their ability to organize, create, and restore. Each scupa has different preferences for what they prefer to repair, ranging from buildings to everyday tools to artwork, and they can rearrange their tail feathers into different patterns.</p><p>When not occupied with work, scupas enjoy puzzles, especially sliding and twisting ones. They are especially fond of puzzles with multiple solutions or that look aesthetically pleasing even in an unsolved state. Scupas enjoy finding non-scupas to share their puzzles and delight in helping others solve their vicious brain teasers.</p><p>Scupas dislike violence, but they recognize that it is sometimes necessary to prevent greater destruction. If their efforts to calm the situation fail, they analyze their foes with the same precision they bring to their beloved crafts before dismantling them into parts.</p><h2>Birds of a Feather</h2><p>Although they look similar to one another, each scupa has a subtly unique tail pattern that they use to identify themselves in social gatherings. Social gatherings between scupas are frequent, as they often like to compare artworks and perform challenging puzzles together. Teams of scupas also come together to quickly repair cities following a disaster or even establish their own art communes in the wild. Although rare, some even join local governments, as scupas are often revered for their innate sense of distance and planning, which makes them excellent city planners.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (heavy), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Crafting, Diplomacy, Lore [Axis], Religion)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, energy resistant (electricity, vitality), force, intelligence, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.4gBIw4IDrSfFHik4]{Daze}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.9HpwDN4MYQJnW0LG]{Dispel Magic}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.dINQzhqGmIsqGMUY]{Mending}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.pwzdSlJgYqN7bs2w]{Telekinetic Hand}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.mrDi3v933gsmnw25]{Telekinetic Maneuver}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{Telekinetic Projectile}), throwing, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Kathryn Kovalcik","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":1},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":5}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":15,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":11,"special":[]},"crafting":{"base":13,"special":[{"label":"to Repair","predicate":["action:repair"],"base":14}]},"diplomacy":{"base":12,"special":[]},"religion":{"base":13,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["monitor"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"SkFYQTSgoKL6b0BM","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/scupa.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Scupa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/scupa.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/scupa.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"name":"Axis Lore","type":"lore","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":13},"proficient":{"value":0}},"effects":[],"_id":"2eCbFW5UBPa8Ts0i","img":"syste